Unity USD Toolkit patch to OpenUSD v26.05 (commit 2095fafafd033fa23386d7ec6d58c7cc33974518), applied
after openusd-26.05-crate-hardening.patch: the Draco file format plugin (usdDraco) in a monolithic
Windows build without Python, and its writer exported on every platform.

Applied by Native~/build_openusd.py to a worktree of the pinned commit, never to the clone itself;
its SHA-256 is pinned in Native~/dependency-sources/<platform>.tsv. Every change is marked
"Unity USD Toolkit" in the source.

1. OpenUSD refuses usdDraco in any monolithic Windows build, in build_usd.py and again in CMake,
   because "this currently results in missing symbols": usdDraco declares no export macros and
   relies on CMAKE_WINDOWS_EXPORT_ALL_SYMBOLS, which does not reach the monolithic library.
   Built without Python, the toolkit's payload links (no unresolved symbol), Draco is static
   inside usd_ms.dll (no new DLL), and the plugin reads .drc files through the file format
   registry from inside the library, as on macOS and Linux. Both checks now refuse the
   combination only with Python enabled.
2. writer.h: UsdDraco_WriteDraco and UsdDraco_PrimvarSupported are declared USDDRACO_API
   (ARCH_EXPORT inside the library, as usdAbc's api.h does), so the toolkit's wrapper can write
   .drc files: the file format cannot (WriteToFile returns false), and in a monolithic Windows
   library the writer was not exported at all. On macOS and Linux it only makes the two
   functions' default visibility explicit.

diff --git a/build_scripts/build_usd.py b/build_scripts/build_usd.py
index 88fb54f..6d3cb55 100644
--- a/build_scripts/build_usd.py
+++ b/build_scripts/build_usd.py
@@ -2622,7 +2622,9 @@ if ZLIB in requiredDependencies:
 
 # Error out if user is building monolithic library on windows with draco plugin
 # enabled. This currently results in missing symbols.
-if context.buildDraco and context.buildMonolithic and Windows():
+# Unity USD Toolkit: only with Python (see cmake/defaults/Options.cmake).
+if (context.buildDraco and context.buildMonolithic and Windows()
+        and context.buildPython):
     PrintError("Draco plugin can not be enabled for monolithic build on Windows")
     sys.exit(1)
 
diff --git a/cmake/defaults/Options.cmake b/cmake/defaults/Options.cmake
index f7211c6..50fc0a2 100644
--- a/cmake/defaults/Options.cmake
+++ b/cmake/defaults/Options.cmake
@@ -230,7 +230,13 @@ endif()
 
 # Error out if user is building monolithic library on windows with draco plugin
 # enabled. This currently results in missing symbols.
-if (${PXR_BUILD_DRACO_PLUGIN} AND ${PXR_BUILD_MONOLITHIC} AND WIN32)
+# Unity USD Toolkit: only with Python. usdDraco declares no export macros
+# beyond its writer (it relies on CMAKE_WINDOWS_EXPORT_ALL_SYMBOLS, which does
+# not reach the monolithic library); without Python only the writer is linked
+# to from outside, and the plugin registers its file format from inside the
+# library.
+if (${PXR_BUILD_DRACO_PLUGIN} AND ${PXR_BUILD_MONOLITHIC} AND WIN32
+    AND ${PXR_ENABLE_PYTHON_SUPPORT})
     message(FATAL_ERROR 
         "Draco plugin can not be enabled for monolithic builds on Windows")
 endif()
diff --git a/pxr/usd/plugin/usdDraco/writer.h b/pxr/usd/plugin/usdDraco/writer.h
index 2ceabca..f141cb2 100644
--- a/pxr/usd/plugin/usdDraco/writer.h
+++ b/pxr/usd/plugin/usdDraco/writer.h
@@ -9,15 +9,29 @@
 #define PXR_USD_PLUGIN_USD_DRACO_WRITER_H
 
 #include "pxr/pxr.h"
+#include "pxr/base/arch/export.h"
 #include "pxr/usd/usdGeom/mesh.h"
 
 #include <string>
 
 
+// Unity USD Toolkit: the writer is exported, as usdAbc's API is, so a program
+// linking the OpenUSD library can write .drc files. usdDraco declared no export
+// macro, which in a monolithic Windows library left it unreachable, and
+// writing is not available through the file format (WriteToFile returns false).
+#if defined(PXR_STATIC)
+#   define USDDRACO_API
+#elif defined(USDDRACO_EXPORTS)
+#   define USDDRACO_API ARCH_EXPORT
+#else
+#   define USDDRACO_API ARCH_IMPORT
+#endif
+
 PXR_NAMESPACE_OPEN_SCOPE
 
 
 /// Encodes mesh and writes it in Draco format to a file at \p fileName.
+USDDRACO_API
 bool UsdDraco_WriteDraco(const UsdGeomMesh &mesh,
                          const std::string &fileName,
                          int qp,
@@ -31,6 +45,7 @@ bool UsdDraco_WriteDraco(const UsdGeomMesh &mesh,
 /// Checks whether a USD primvar can be encoded to Draco. It is called from
 /// usdcompress.py script to determine whether a primvar should be deleted from
 /// USD mesh or remain in USD mesh.
+USDDRACO_API
 bool UsdDraco_PrimvarSupported(const UsdGeomPrimvar &primvar);
 
 
